      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is relevant when recording skits/etc. Currently, for the audio volume/panning to match the camera, the player recording must essentially keep their head glued to the camera, or the 3D audio will sound wrong to the viewer. \nI've seen a demo of multiple audio listeners operating together, though it might not work in VRChat. If not, it would still be a useful feature that could be toggled on (swap between head listener and camera listener)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
